{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T3kZjNYCDVxGajxNA6LnH6","type":"tool_result","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D28 seen vs. D29+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-28 after D28 (single 1703 ids = +44, 179 members; \"Out of Order\" / base `terraform-cloud-timeline` added 4\n`polyglot-terraform_hcl-*.tf`, NO host, no new bash -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `terraform { required_version =\n\">= 1.0\" }`, `locals { huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"<data>\" }`, `output \"inert_analysis_<8hex>\" { value =\nlocal.huntress_descriptor_<8hex> }`; no resources/providers/depends_on/timestamps). Carried D23 solver answered everything\nunpatched: single CORRECT ~T+49 s (race win, 0 wrong), TT 1781 and Mastery (**12 sets**, 21372) first try. **The timed contract\nflipped BACK to the per-file grammar** (D23-D26 shape: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, 13 ids per polyglot member, LYR tags,\n`<colour>_<shape>` stage_profile) and **the next_language pool is back** without terraform_hcl: 5/5 hits (jsp, elixir, erlang,\ndockerfile, terraform_hcl each left the pool the day it shipped). Pool left (12, 3 days D29-D31): awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin,\nmakefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh -- so either several languages land per day, or some never ship. The D27\nsibling bet (Makefile) MISSED. Prompt (\"Assemble the timeline from resources, prior scripts, and relationship evidence ...\nfind the change that happened out of order\") was never asked -- 15th narrative in a row. Prebuild after D27 night built every\nqueued script gap except make-recipe-inner-scripts (1 failed try): makefile-v3-carrier-forms, var-interpolation-concat-fold,\nfunction-return-literal-battery, specimen-lineage-attribution, terraform-hcl-v3-fixtures, xslt-v3-fixtures,\nbuild-file-host-profiles, v3-tag-vocab-extend, shell-rc-host-carriers, dockerfile-multistage-stage-graph,\ncorpus-aggregate-questions.\nRead with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n  D18 solve.py and in lib.codec since D18 night). **D19 broke the raw-bytes assumption**: the ASPX host carries the whole\n  inner script as an escaped string literal (`\\n`, `\\\"`), so marker data runs into `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is\n  `\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). D20 had no carrier twist. The real D21+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n  -- yet (nor D19-D21's). D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host),\n  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`), jenkins_pipeline + classic_asp (D20; classic_asp wraps\n  VBScript = first host for a PRIOR language, first day with two host files); D21 GitHub Actions came as a LANGUAGE\n  (`polyglot-github_actions`, profile standalone), not a host. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: fake \"Decrypt document\" lure), D19 .NET (Roslyn\n  C# script + ASPX inline host; base id `managed-assembly-bridge`), D20 the JVM/CI side (Groovy + Jenkins pipeline; prompt\n  \"controller vs agent semantics ... trace the modeled build into its prior-language stages\" -- never asked), D21 GitHub\n  Actions YAML (base `github-actions-persistence`; \"trigger and trust boundary ... the job that keeps coming back\" -- never\n  asked), D22 NSIS installer script (base `installer-script-chain`; \"setup actions vs payload, every cross-language\n  handoff\" -- never asked). Three threads now run: (c) **installers/packaging** (NSIS seen D22 -> Inno Setup `.iss` Pascal\n  `[Code]`, WiX `.wxs`/MSI CustomAction scripts, compiled NSIS/Inno exes, `.inf`, deb/rpm maintainer scripts, macOS `.pkg`\n  Distribution JS, Chocolatey/Scoop/winget manifests, MSIX/ClickOnce/Squirrel); (a) **build/CI supply-chain hosts** (Jenkins -> GitHub Actions (seen D21) -> GitLab/Azure YAML, Gradle `.kts`, Makefile/Docker,\n  npm/pip lifecycle hooks, VS Code tasks) whose steps embed PRIOR languages (`sh`/`bat`/`powershell` bodies); (b) **hosts for\n  prior languages** (classic ASP VBS -> ASP JScript, WSC, Jupyter Python, systemd/cron Bash, Electron Node, NSE Lua).\n  Languages still unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Kotlin/Java/Scala/Clojure, Tcl, Go, Rust, R, F#/VB.NET, GitLab/\n  Azure/CircleCI YAML, Kubernetes/Helm, Terraform/CloudFormation, Ansible, Makefile/Docker, Swift/JXA, Dart. Carrier twists so\n  far: D18 layout (SPLIT array), D19 nesting (escaped inner file), D20-D21 none -- a third (assembled strings, YAML block/\n  folded scalars or anchors, JSON-escaped notebook/manifest, compiled bytes) is still due. Base ids name a THEME the bytes\n  don't carry yet (D19 bridge, D20 intrusion, D21 persistence): when one finally ships semantics (triggers, schedules,\n  loci), the questions will be new suffixes -- `lib.codec.plan_answer` first, then the theme readers (gaps below).\n- ~3 drops left (D29-D31). D28 = Terraform HCL (pool language, NOT the Makefile sibling; `locals`+`output` indirection like\n  D27's ARG/LABEL; timed back to per-file + pool). D27 = Dockerfile (thread (a) build/CI; sibling Makefile still unshipped; ARG+LABEL carrier,\n  no host; timed contract back to the single grammar). D26 = Erlang escript (BEAM sibling of D25, no host; nameless `build_plan() -> \"..\"`). D25 = Elixir + Phoenix web host (BEAM; web-host thread again after D24 JSP; first prompt that NAMED\n  its language). D24 went back to thread (b)/web hosts (JSP = JVM webshell; sibling of D8 php_webshell, D19 ASPX,\n  D20 classic ASP, D20 Groovy). Strongest predictor D24-D28 is the timed `next_language` pool (5/5; hidden on D27's semantic timed day, back on D28). D23 opened a fourth thread: (d) **game engines / modding** (Godot GDScript seen D23 -> Godot\n  `.tscn`/`.tres` resources with embedded `script/source`, `.pck` packs, Roblox Luau, Ren'Py `.rpy`/`.rpyc`, GameMaker GML,\n  Squirrel `.nut`, AngelScript, Pawn, Minecraft `.mcfunction`/datapacks, UnrealScript/Blueprint text, Unity C#). And the\n  timed-contract grammar is now a moving part on its own: expect the single to adopt the per-file shape, more LYR layer names,\n  and more cross-file (corpus) questions.\n  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804d4269-9c1b-478e-a2b8-4da32f300eac","uuid":"745eba13-bf89-4dc0-89ed-23428413c6f6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:40:36.166Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D28 seen vs. D29+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-28 after D28 (single 1703 ids = +44, 179 members; \"Out of Order\" / base `terraform-cloud-timeline` added 4\n`polyglot-terraform_hcl-*.tf`, NO host, no new bash -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `terraform { required_version =\n\">= 1.0\" }`, `locals { huntress_d