red days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix); D26-D28 had none. If a pool language brings one, likely wrappers: Kotlin `build.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { .. } }`), BeanShell inside a JMeter `.jmx` (XML-escaped `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` -> NESTED carrier with `&quot;`/`&#xa;`), Swift `Package.swift`, Nim `.nimble` tasks, Tcl `expect` script, XSLT run by `wmic os get /format:` (Squiblytwo), zsh/fish rc files (built: shell-rc-host-carriers). host_profile spellings follow `<tool>_<kind>` (fixture guesses only: gradle_build, jmeter_beanshell, swift_package, wmic_xsl) -- answers stay plan-verbatim; route by marker. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside each wrapper incl. one XML-entity-escaped JMX; assert lib.codec.v3_plan unescapes and rescans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"descriptor-decode-call-wrapper\", \"concept\": \"descriptor literal wrapped in the host language's own decode call (marker kept or dropped)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27/D28 split declaration from use; the next step is the literal inside a decode expression: HCL `base64decode(\\\"..\\\")`/`jsondecode`, Kotlin/BeanShell `String(Base64.getDecoder().decode(\\\"..\\\"))`, Swift `Data(base64Encoded: \\\"..\\\")`, Nim `decode(\\\"..\\\")` (std/base64), Rust `STANDARD.decode(\\\"..\\\")`, Tcl `binary decode base64 {..}`, zsh/fish `$(print -r -- .. | base64 -d)` / `echo .. | base64 -d`, XSLT none. Prebuild in lib.codec: recognise these call shapes, take the argument literal, apply the named decode before the shape peel (count it as a layer), accept only `v=`. Fixtures with and without the line-1 marker; assert the marker plan wins when both exist.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"make-recipe-inner-scripts\", \"concept\": \"build-file recipes/RUN lines that embed PRIOR-language scripts (bash, PowerShell, Python, Node) as a handoff\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 Dockerfile shipped only FROM/ARG/LABEL, but the build-file theme invites `RUN` / recipe bodies carrying earlier languages: Dockerfile `RUN <<EOF ... EOF` heredocs, `RUN [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` exec form, `SHELL [\\\"powershell\\\",\\\"-Command\\\"]`, `RUN echo <b64> | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `SHELL := pwsh`, `.ONESHELL:` multi-line recipes, `$(shell python3 -c '..')`, `\\\\`-continued recipe lines, `@` / `-` prefixes. Prebuild lib.codec.build_inner_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language, script_text)] (Dockerfile instruction / make target, interpreter from SHELL or the command head, `$$` -> `$` unescaped), then route each inner script to the existing analysers (lib.codec.v3_plan / find_codecs). Fixtures: a marker+plan only inside a RUN heredoc and only inside a .ONESHELL recipe. Never docker build / make. Still pending after D28 (1 failed try): Makefile is still in the D28 pool; also extract Terraform `local-exec` command bodies through the same interface.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"change-order-anomaly\", \"concept\": \"'find the change that happened out of order' -- ordering anomalies over plans/handoffs (D28 prompt; never asked)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 prompt asked to 'assemble the timeline ... and find the change that happened out of order'; nothing shipped (15th narrative). If a question comes, the evidence in the corpus is: plan `steps` order vs the canonical role order (acquire_remote before dispatch_*, decode_* before write_file before dispatch_process), stage_count vs len(steps), next_language/next_stage handoff edges vs member order, and any timestamps (zip member mtimes -- all fixed 2026-01-01 so far -- or plan keys like `created=`/`seq=`). Prebuild lib.codec.order_anomalies(plans_by_member, zip_infos=None) -> [(member, kind, evidence)] per Mastery set; answer shapes to expect: member file name, step token, integer position. Fixtures: one member with swapped steps, one with a handoff pointing backwards.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hcl-resource-dependency-timeline\", \"concept\": \"Terraform resource graph (references, depends_on, count/for_each, provisioners) ordered into a timeline\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 Terraform shipped only `terraform{}`/`locals{}`/`output{}`; the prompt's 'resources, expressions, and dependencies that change over time' suggests a later delivery could add `resource \\\"terraform_data\\\"`/`null_resource` blocks with `depends_on`, `triggers_replace`, `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\"`, `lifecycle { create_before_destroy }`, and expression references `local.x`/`resource.y.id`. Prebuild lib.codec.hcl_blocks(text) (brace-aware, heredoc `<<-EOT` aware, comments `#`/`//`/`/* */`) -> [{type, labels, attrs, refs}] and hcl_order(blocks) -> topological order + edges that contradict file order. Never terraform init/plan. Feeds change-order-anomaly and make/embedded-script extraction (local-exec command bodies).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try. D26 10 sets, D27 11 sets (semantic ids `setN.<lang>-<role>-<field>`); first try both days. D28: 12 sets, per-file ids again (`set1.polyglot-terraform_hcl-767e8f-..`), first try.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids). D26: unchanged a 4th time (TT 1677). **D27: REVERTED to the single's semantic grammar** (TT 1659 = single, Mastery 11 x 1659 = 18249, no 6hex stems, no LYR tags, no colour_shape stage_profile, next_language only base languages); the carried solver handled it because it keeps both grammars. Never delete the semantic path when a reshape lands; expect a further flip either way on D28-D31. **D28: flipped BACK to per-file** (TT 1781 = D26 1677 + 52 dockerfile + 52 terraform_hcl; Mastery 12 x 1781 = 21372; LYR tags, colour_shape stage_profile and the next_language pool all back); carried solver answered it unpatched. The grammar is chosen per day -- keep both paths and the answered-ratio check.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"forecast the next language from the timed next_language pool (5/5 D24-D28; hidden on D27's semantic timed day)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Hits: jsp -> D24, elixir -> D25, erlang -> D26, dockerfile -> D27, terraform_hcl -> D28 (each left the pool the day it shipped). D27 timed was semantic and showed only base languages; D28 per-file timed showed the pool again: 12 left = awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh (3 days D29-D31 -> multi-language days or some never ship). The D27 sibling bet (Makefile) MISSED: prefer the pool over family pairs. Re-read only TODAY's auto-* expected.json `-next-language` values nightly (older cases carry stale pools); a language that leaves the pool without shipping = it shipped in a timed-only form or the pool was re-rolled.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-scale-final-days\", \"concept\": \"Mastery growth to 13-15 sets (+ multi-language days) vs the solve/submit budget\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D28 Mastery c4556fc4: 12 sets x 1781 = 21372 ids, solve 3.5 s, submit 6.2 s (submit now dominates), total 10.1 s. D31 could be 15 sets x ~1900-2100 = ~30k ids: keep one submit (GM: up to 4 MiB of JSON per request; split only above), fork per set, never re-index nested AES zips per set. If total approaches the window, profile the submit serialisation before the solver.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D28: the D28 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs .escript .dockerfile .tf (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members). D26: `polyglot-erlang` (ERLANG-), no host. D27: `polyglot-dockerfile` (campaign DOCKERFILE-, url host dockerfile-.., /tmp/huntress-dockerfile/), no host; D28: `polyglot-terraform_hcl` (campaign TERRAFORM_HCL-, url host terraform_hcl-.., /tmp/huntress-terraform_hcl/), no host; per-file timed `polyglot-terraform_hcl-<6hex>-<field>`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804d4269-9c1b-478e-a2b8-4da32f300eac","uuid":"19b7fe8c-889f-4af0-928a-d11a11da2b7a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:40:36.905Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS .scpt | MEI\\x0c/PYZ pyinstaller | 0d0d0a pyc | #@~^ Script-Encoder -> wshenc\nSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:  stages: -> GitLab  pool: -> Azure  kind: -> k8s  - hosts: -> ansible  $CHICAGO$ -> .inf\n #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n onOpen_ / DocumentApp / HtmlService / showSidebar / UrlFetchApp -> Google Apps Script (D18; polyglot-google_apps_script)\n ExcelScript./Office.onReady -> Office add-in  \"manifest_version\" -> browser ext  set x \"v\"/proc -> tcl  x <- v -> R  := -> go\n fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   final String x= / def f = { -> / pipeline{ -> groovy (D20)\n BEGIN{ / getline -> awk     target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell / define..endef -> make (pool)     FROM .. AS / ARG / LABEL -> Dockerfile (D27)\n on:/jobs:/runs-on: + `# HUNTRESS..` line 1 + env HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR (no id) -> GH Actions (D21; polyglot-github_actions)\n Name/OutFile/Section + StrCpy $0 \"..\" + `;` marker -> NSIS (D22)  [Setup]/[Code] -> Inno  <Wix>/CustomAction -> WiX/MSI\n terraform{ + locals{ huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\" } + output{ value = local.x } -> terraform_hcl (D28)  Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild   <%@ Page/runat=\"server\" -> ASPX (D19)   <%@ Language=VBScript %> -> classic ASP (D20)\n <%! String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#`+descriptor_x = +%{..} -> elixir (D25)  `%`+-module(+build_plan() -> \"..\". (no name) -> erlang (D26)\n extends RefCounted / const X: String = / func f() -> Dictionary: / `#` marker -> GDScript (D23)  [gd_scene/[gd_resource -> Godot\n resource (script/source = \"escaped\")  GDPC -> .pck  label start:/init python: -> Ren'Py  game:GetService -> Luau  @\"..\" -> Squirrel\n host-<profile>-<lang> may wrap an OLD language (D20 classic_asp VBScript in a .vbs): marker first, plan says language=\n Sub AutoOpen/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA  =EXEC( -> XLM  __EventFilter -> MOF  #nullable/BuildPlan_ => -> csx (D19)  let/|> -> fsx\nPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`.\n marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n D23 `LYR-<l1>_<l2>_<l3>-data` = ENCODE layers (b64 b32 hex rev frag): undo last-first; obfuscation answer = layer string\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code or a known list\nTIMED CONTRACT GRAMMAR: D23-D26 ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` over `<6hex>.<ext>` members -> route by field; composite fields =\n labels joined by `|` in the question's order; indicator = first present in the question's order; campaign-token = after 1st\n `-`; url-host/path-leaf from plan url/file_path; cross-file ids (handoff-id) resolved PER MASTERY SET. Diff id grammar first.\n Flips DAILY: D27 timed = semantic ids (no LYR, no pool); D28 per-file again (TT 1781, M 12x1781, LYR + pool) -- keep BOTH.\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper | Python: exec->print under python3 -I, marshal->pycdc\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER run the fixture's interpreter (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File), Deparse/`make -n` (they execute), XSLT, plan URLs.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\nNARRATIVE prompts D16-D28 (network/process/outlier/drift/flow/decoy/lineage/timeline): flavour 15/15 unless asked; then\n lib.codec network_indicators+reconcile, download_graph, reconcile_processes, lineage, corpus_summary.\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..Terraform).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D26 nights (see git history) and D27 night\nmakefile-v3-carrier-forms, var-interpolation-concat-fold, function-return-literal-battery, specimen-lineage-attribution,\nterraform-hcl-v3-fixtures, xslt-v3-fixtures, build-file-host-profiles, v3-tag-vocab-extend, shell-rc-host-carriers,\ndockerfile-multistage-stage-graph, corpus-aggregate-questions. Every one of the 12 pool languages now has single-shape fixtures\n(zsh/fish, awk/sed, nim/swift/tcl, kotlin/beanshell, makefile, xslt, rust). Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\nevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route,\nawk-sed-program-route, composite-label-field-regime. Prebuild rules learned: only hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no\n`__import__`, no `tomllib`); keep fixtures tiny (other lanes' slow fixtures under load have sunk script-lane attempts).\nPriority-1 order for D29: 12 pool languages / 3 days -> a MULTI-language drop through the carried solver in BOTH timed grammars\n(the D28 per-file flip landed new families straight into `<6hex>` ids + LYR), then a prior-language script embedded inside the\nnew file (the D28 prompt's \"prior scripts and relationship evidence\"); then LYR vocabulary, pool-language hosts, decode-call\nwrappers, make recipes; the D28 \"out of order\" narrative readers last.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"multi-language-drop-battery\", \"concept\": \"2-4 never-shipped pool languages landing on ONE day, answered end-to-end by the carried solver in both timed grammars\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 left 12 pool languages (awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh) for 3 days (D29-D31): a multi-language day is likely. Per-language single-shape fixtures exist (built D23-D27 nights) but nothing runs a whole CONTRACT. Prebuild a synthetic case generator + fixtures: 3 new families in the D28 layout (line-1 `<comment> HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, a header block, a named `huntress_descriptor_<8hex>` literal, an indirect use like D28 `output { value = local.x }` / D27 `LABEL ..=$X`), rendered as (a) a semantic contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<role>-<field>`, 11 fields) and (b) a per-file contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<6hex>-<field>`, 13 fields incl. url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token, LYR-tagged markers). Assert 100% answered by lib.codec.v3_plan + plan_answer for underscore-free and underscore families, campaign-token = after the FIRST hyphen (`TERRAFORM_HCL-10a06eec` -> `10a06eec`), url-host keeps `_`. Stdlib only; tiny fixtures.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"embedded-prior-script-dual-plan\", \"concept\": \"a new-language file that embeds a PRIOR-language fixture (its own Codec_/v=1-2 plan) next to its own v=3 marker\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 prompt: 'Assemble the timeline from resources, prior scripts, and relationship evidence' -- prior scripts were never embedded yet, but D19 ASPX already nested a whole inner file. Expect e.g. Terraform `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT }` / Makefile recipe / Kotlin raw string `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / XSLT CDATA / fish `begin; ..; end` holding a PowerShell/bash/batch fixture with `Codec_<id>`/`Material_<id>`. Prebuild lib.codec.embedded_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language_guess, inner_text)] (heredoc/raw-string/CDATA/escaped-string extraction, unescape `\\\\n \\\\\\\" $$ &quot;`), and a selector: the OUTER file's v=3 marker plan answers its polyglot ids; inner plans are returned separately for new suffixes (`-inner-*`, `-prior-*`, `-next-stage`) via plan_answer. Fixtures: same file with outer B64 marker + inner PS FromBase64String descriptor + inner bash Codec_; assert the outer plan is never replaced by the inner one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lyr-layer-vocab-extend\", \"concept\": \"timed LYR-<layers> tags with layer names beyond b64/b32/hex/rev/frag\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 timed brought LYR back (1-3 layers of b64/b32/hex/rev/frag, encode order, obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim, e.g. `b32_rev_b64`). v3-tag-vocab-extend (built) covers SINGLE tags only. A late twist could add layers (`b85`/`a85`, `z`/`zlib`, `gz`, `rot13`, `url`, `u16`, `xor<hex>`, 4+ deep). Prebuild: extend the tag-directed peel with a layer table + shape-peel fallback for an unknown layer name (try each known decoder at that position, accept only a final `v=`), and keep the obfuscation answer = the raw tag text. Fixtures for each new layer in `#`, `//`, `--`, `<!-- -->`, `%` comments, 4-deep stacks; must stay inside the 2 s budget.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pool-language-host-wrappers\", \"concept\": \"HOST profiles for the remaining pool languages (Gradle, JMeter BeanShell, Package.swift, nimble, Expect, wmic XSL)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hosts shipped only on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix); D26-D28 had none. If a pool language brings one, likely wrappers: Kotlin `build.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { .. } }`), BeanShell inside a JMeter `.jmx` (XML-escaped `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` -> NESTED carrier with `&quot;`/`&#xa;`), Swift `Package.swift`, Nim `.nimble` tasks, Tcl `expect` script, XSLT run by `wmic os get /format:` (Squiblytwo), zsh/fish rc files (built: shell-rc-host-carriers). host_profile spellings follow `<tool>_<kind>` (fixture guesses only: gradle_build, jmeter_beanshell, swift_package, wmic_xsl) -- answers stay plan-verbatim; route by marker. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside each wrapper incl. one XML-entity-escaped JMX; assert lib.codec.v3_plan unescapes and rescans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"descriptor-decode-call-wrapper\", \"concept\": \"descriptor literal wrapped in the host language's own decode call (marker kept or dropped)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27/D28 split declaration from use; the next step is the literal inside a decode expression: HCL `base64decode(\\\"..\\\")`/`jsondecode`, Kotlin/BeanShell `String(Base64.getDecoder().decode(\\\"..\\\"))`, Swift `Data(base64Encoded: \\\"..\\\")`, Nim `decode(\\\"..\\\")` (std/base64), Rust `STANDARD.decode(\\\"..\\\")`, Tcl `binary decode base64 {..}`, zsh/fish `$(print -r -- .. | base64 -d)` / `echo .. | base64 -d`, XSLT none. Prebuild in lib.codec: recognise these call shapes, take the argument literal, apply the named decode before the shape peel (count it as a layer), accept only `v=`. Fixtures with and without the line-1 marker; assert the marker plan wins when both exist.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"make-recipe-inner-scripts\", \"concept\": \"build-file recipes/RUN lines that embed PRIOR-language scripts (bash, PowerShell, Python, Node) as a handoff\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 Dockerfile shipped only FROM/ARG/LABEL, but the build-file theme invites `RUN` / recipe bodies carrying earlier languages: Dockerfile `RUN <<EOF ... EOF` heredocs, `RUN [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` exec form, `SHELL [\\\"powershell\\\",\\\"-Command\\\"]`, `RUN echo <b64> | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `SHELL := pwsh`, `.ONESHELL:` multi-line recipes, `$(shell python3 -c '..')`, `\\\\`-continued recipe lines, `@` / `-` prefixes. Prebuild lib.codec.build_inner_scripts(text) -> [(locus, language, script_text)] (Dockerfile instruction / make target, interpreter from SHELL or the command head, `$$` -> `$` unescaped), then route each inner script to the existing analysers (lib.codec.v3_plan / find_codecs). Fixtures: a marker+plan only inside a RUN heredoc and only inside a .ONESHELL recipe. Never docker build / make. Still pending after D28 (1 failed try): Makefile is still in the D28 pool; also extract Terraform `local-exec` command bodies through the same interface.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"change-order-anomaly\", \"concept\": \"'find the change that happened out of order' -- ordering anomalies over plans/handoffs (D28 prompt; never asked)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 prompt asked to 'assemble the timeline ... and find the change that happened out of order'; nothing shipped (15th narrative). If a question comes, the evidence in the corpus is: plan `steps` order vs the canonical role order (acquire_remote before dispatch_*, decode_* before write_file before dispatch_process), stage_count vs len(steps), next_language/next_stage handoff edges vs member order, and any timestamps (zip member mtimes -- all fixed 2026-01-01 so far -- or plan keys like `created=`/`seq=`). Prebuild lib.codec.order_anomalies(plans_by_member, zip_infos=None) -> [(member, kind, evidence)] per Mastery set; answer shapes to expect: member file name, step token, integer position. Fixtures: one member with swapped steps, one with a handoff pointing backwards.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hcl-resource-dependency-timeline\", \"concept\": \"Terraform resource graph (references, depends_on, count/for_each, provisioners) ordered into a timeline\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 Terraform shipped only `terraform{}`/`locals{}`/`output{}`; the prompt's 'resources, expressions, and dependencies that change over time' suggests a later delivery could add `resource \\\"terraform_data\\\"`/`null_resource` blocks with `depends_on`, `triggers_replace`, `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\"`, `lifecycle { create_before_destroy }`, and expression references `local.x`/`resource.y.id`. Prebuild lib.codec.hcl_blocks(text) (brace-aware, heredoc `<<-EOT` aware, comments `#`/`//`/`/* */`) -> [{type, labels, attrs, refs}] and hcl_order(blocks) -> topological order + edges that contradict file order. Never terraform init/plan. Feeds change-order-anomaly and make/embedded-script extraction (local-exec command bodies).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try). D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try. D26 10 sets, D27 11 sets (semantic ids `setN.<lang>-<role>-<field>`); first try both days. D28: 12 sets, per-file ids again (`set1.polyglot-terraform_hcl-767e8f-..`), first try.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape. D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids). D26: unchanged a 4th time (TT 1677). **D27: REVERTED to the single's semantic grammar** (TT 1659 = single, Mastery 11 x 1659 = 18249, no 6hex stems, no LYR tags, no colour_shape stage_profile, next_language only base languages); the carried solver handled it because it keeps both grammars. Never delete the semantic path when a reshape lands; expect a further flip either way on D28-D31. **D28: flipped BACK to per-file** (TT 1781 = D26 1677 + 52 dockerfile + 52 terraform_hcl; Mastery 12 x 1781 = 21372; LYR tags, colour_shape stage_profile and the next_language pool all back); carried solver answered it unpatched. The grammar is chosen per day -- keep both paths and the answered-ratio check.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"forecast the next language from the timed next_language pool (5/5 D24-D28; hidden on D27's semantic timed day)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Hits: jsp -> D24, elixir -> D25, erlang -> D26, dockerfile -> D27, terraform_hcl -> D28 (each left the pool the day it shipped). D27 timed was semantic and showed only base languages; D28 per-file timed showed the pool again: 12 left = awk, beanshell, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh (3 days D29-D31 -> multi-language days or some never ship). The D27 sibling bet (Makefile) MISSED: prefer the pool over family pairs. Re-read only TODAY's auto-* expected.json `-next-language` values nightly (older cases carry stale pools); a language that leaves the pool without shipping = it shipped in a timed-only form or the pool was re-rolled.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-scale-final-days\", \"concept\": \"Mastery growth to 13-15 sets (+ multi-language days) vs the solve/submit budget\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D28 Mastery c4556fc4: 12 sets x 1781 = 21372 ids, solve 3.5 s, submit 6.2 s (submit now dominates), total 10.1 s. D31 could be 15 sets x ~1900-2100 = ~30k ids: keep one submit (GM: up to 4 MiB of JSON per request; split only above), fork per set, never re-index nested AES zips per set. If total approaches the window, profile the submit serialisation before the solver.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D28: the D28 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs .escript .dockerfile .tf (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members). D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members). D26: `polyglot-erlang` (ERLANG-), no host. D27: `polyglot-dockerfile` (campaign DOCKERFILE-, url host dockerfile-.., /tmp/huntress-dockerfile/), no host; D28: `polyglot-terraform_hcl` (campaign TERRAFORM_HCL-, url host terraform_hcl-.., /tmp/huntress-terraform_hcl/), no host; per-file timed `polyglot-terraform_hcl-<6hex>-<field>`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TyNQZSKWFZRiHDB3FGvq8w","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
