{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdD7KFxRmuS5m9AQXP5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LwbTU4VTMKP1TCTkx691ni","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ng0=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nj0=s.index('```json',g0); j1=s.index('```',j0+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j0+7:j1])\nby={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nbuilt={'embedded-prior-script-dual-plan','lyr-layer-vocab-extend','pool-language-host-wrappers','descriptor-decode-call-wrapper','make-recipe-inner-scripts','change-order-anomaly','hcl-resource-dependency-timeline'}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"corpus-language-graph-bridge\",\"concept\":\"'find the edge that holds everything together' -- bridge/articulation edge of the corpus execution+host+evidence graph\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 prompt (base `beanshell-jsp-graph`): 'rebuild the complete execution, host, and evidence graph, and find the edge that holds everything together' -- never asked on D30, but D31 is the finale and 30 languages are now 'complete'. lib.codec.handoff_graph (built) already gives per-member next-stage edges; extend it: lib.codec.corpus_graph(plans_by_member, texts_by_member, set_scope) -> nodes = members AND languages; edges typed `execution` (plan next_language / next_stage / PS `$HandoffId`->python handoff_id), `host` (host_profile container -> inner language: classic_asp->vbscript, jsp_beanshell = jsp->beanshell, aspx_inline_csharp->csharp_script, jenkins_pipeline->groovy, wsf/hta/sct->jscript|vbscript, php_webshell, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, elixir_phoenix, jsp_webshell), `evidence` (shared campaign token / url host / file_path between members). Then graph_answer(g, question): bridges (Tarjan, edge whose removal disconnects), articulation points, max-betweenness edge, in/out degree, connected-component count, the language reached by most chains. Answer shapes to support: `src>dst` (ordered_tokens), member file name, language name, integer. Per Mastery set. Fixtures: a 6-member toy corpus with one bridge edge (host jsp->beanshell) and one cycle; assert bridge, articulation, counts. Stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"capstone-new-suffix-on-old-families\",\"concept\":\"finale contract with NO new language but new question suffixes on existing families (graph/host/consensus fields)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If D31 ships no 31st language (the D30 prompt closed a 'thirty-language puzzle'), the only new ids will be new FIELD suffixes on old families or one corpus-level family (e.g. `corpus-*`, `graph-*`, `capstone-*`, `<family>-host-language`, `-inner-language`, `-parent`, `-edge`, `-bridge`, `-degree`, `-component`). Prebuild a router in lib.codec: for an id the carried solver leaves unanswered, (1) plan_answer (longest plan-key suffix), (2) corpus_graph/graph_answer for graph words in the question (edge, bridge, connect, holds together, path, parent, child, reachable), (3) corpus_summary/corpus_answer for counts, (4) lineage for parent/attribution, (5) else NO answer (never guess into a bulk). Fixtures: a contract JSON with 6 such synthetic ids over a toy corpus; assert routing and that unknowns stay unanswered. Speed: whole-contract pass < 0.5 s.\"},\n {\"id\":\"double-nested-host-carrier\",\"concept\":\"host inside host: a script escaped twice (e.g. WSF/HTA/JSP holding an ASPX/JSP that holds the script) -> unescape twice\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Nesting grew D19 (ASPX -> C# escaped once) and D30 (JSP -> BeanShell escaped once, `INERT_BEANSHELL_<8HEX> = \\\"// HUNTRESS..\\\\\\\\n..\\\\\\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\"`). A capstone could stack two seen hosts (jsp_webshell -> jsp_beanshell, classic_asp -> wsf_jscript, jenkins_pipeline -> groovy -> bsh): marker text then appears with DOUBLE escapes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `&amp;quot;`, CDATA inside an escaped string). Prebuild: make lib.codec.v3_plan unescape iteratively (up to 3 rounds of `\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\uXXXX`, `\\\"\\\"`, `&quot;`/`&amp;`, CDATA strip) until a marker peels to `v=`; return the INNERMOST plan for the file's ids and the host chain (outer->inner profiles) for graph questions. Fixtures: 2-deep JSP-in-JSP, VBS-in-WSF-in-HTA, with FRAG and HB64 tags; assert one plan, correct host chain.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mastery-scale-bench-30k\",\"concept\":\"Mastery at 15 sets x ~1900-2000 ids (~28-30k) inside the timed budget\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Mastery grew +1 set/day: D28 12 x 1781 (solve 3.5 s), D29 13 x 1833 (5.7 s), D30 14 x 1898 = 26572 (solve 7.25 s, submit 5.9 s, total 14.0 s) -- solve time doubled in two days. D31 likely 15 sets (~28.5k, more if a language lands). Prebuild a synthetic bench (tiny fixtures replicated into a 15-set nested AES-free zip shape the solver accepts) that times the per-set analyse path and the answer-JSON serialisation, flags any per-member O(n^2) (e.g. per-member full-corpus scans in corpus/handoff lookups) and memoises per CONTENT sha256 within a process (never by id(obj): D25). Target: solve <= 5 s for 15 sets on an idle box. Report the top 5 hot functions; no network.\"},\n {\"id\":\"next-language-member-resolve\",\"concept\":\"resolve a plan's next_language / next_stage to the concrete member it hands off to (same set)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 host plan: next_language = a PRIOR language (jscript) with stage_profile cross_language_handoff; D23 already asked one cross-file id (`python-<6hex>-handoff-id`). A graph question will need the TARGET member, not just the language: rank candidate members of that language in the same Mastery set by shared campaign token / url host / file_path stem / handoff id / role (staged_chain -> launcher|downloader), tie-break by file name. Prebuild lib.codec.resolve_handoff(member, plan, plans_by_member) -> (member_name, evidence) and wire it into handoff_graph; answers: member file name or `<6hex>.<ext>` stem in per-file mode. Fixtures: 2 jscript candidates, one sharing the campaign token; assert the right one.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-variant-consensus\",\"concept\":\"'keep only the conclusions that hold up across every variant' -- per-field consensus across Mastery sets / variants\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D29 prompt (base `makefile-variant-diff`): 'Diff them carefully, and keep only the tradecraft conclusions that hold up across every variant.' Never asked, but Mastery ships N sets of the same member stems with re-rolled values. Prebuild lib.codec.variant_consensus(plans_by_set) -> per (family, role) the fields whose value is identical in every set (role, attack, adapter, steps, host_profile, stage_profile typically stable; campaign/url/path re-roll) and the fields that differ; answer shapes: field name list joined by `|`/`,`, the invariant value, or the member that breaks consensus. Fixtures: 3 sets x 2 members with one deliberately divergent role.\"},\n {\"id\":\"analysis-v2-marker-schema\",\"concept\":\"a finale schema bump: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V2:` marker or `v=4` plan with new keys (edges, parent, host_language, inner)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The marker has been `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1` with plan `v=3` since D8; a capstone could bump it. Prebuild: accept `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\\\d+` (already) AND plans starting `v=4`/`v=5`, values containing `;`/`>`/`,` lists (`edges=a>b;b>c`, `parents=..`), nested `k:v` pairs, or a JSON object; plan_answer maps new keys generically (hyphen<->underscore, plural/singular), list values joined in the question's stated separator. Fixtures: V2 marker + v=4 plan with edges list in `#`, `//`, `<%-- --%>` hosts; assert all keys reachable and v=3 parsing unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"graph-evidence-file-reconcile\",\"concept\":\"a shipped graph evidence file (edges JSON/CSV, DOT, GraphML, Mermaid) to reconcile against plan-derived edges\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17-D18 prompts named second evidence types that never shipped; D30 named an 'evidence graph'. If the finale ships one, it will be e.g. `graph.json` {nodes, edges:[{src,dst,kind}]}, `edges.csv`, `*.dot` (`a -> b [label=..]`), `*.graphml`, or Mermaid `A --> B`. Prebuild lib.codec.graph_evidence(path_or_text) -> normalised edge set (lowercased member/language names, kind) and reconcile_edges(declared=corpus_graph edges, observed) -> only-declared / only-observed / mismatched-kind edges. Fixtures: one of each format (tiny) with one one-sided edge; never render or execute anything.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mixed-grammar-single-contract\",\"concept\":\"one contract mixing the semantic (`<lang>-<role>-<field>`) and per-file (`<family>-<6hex>-<field>`) id grammars\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Timed grammar flipped D23 per-file -> D27 semantic -> D28-D30 per-file; the single stayed semantic. A finale could merge them (semantic ids for old members, `<6hex>` ids for new ones, or `setN.` prefixes on a single). Today the solver picks ONE grammar per contract. Prebuild a per-ID grammar router: classify each id independently (per-file iff the 6hex stem matches a member stem in the same set), answer each through its own path, and report the answered ratio per grammar. Fixtures: a contract with 50/50 mixed ids over 4 members; assert 100% answered and no cross-grammar collisions (`-campaign` vs `-campaign-token`).\"},\n]\nmlb=by['multi-language-drop-battery']\nmlb['priority']=2\nmlb['detail']=\"Pool after D30: 10 never-shipped languages (awk, fish, kotlin, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh) and ONE day left; the organizers shipped exactly one per day through D30 and the D30 prompt closed a 'thirty-language puzzle', so a finale multi-drop is possible but not the base case. Per-language single-shape fixtures exist (built D23-D27 nights) but nothing runs a whole CONTRACT. Prebuild a synthetic case generator + fixtures: 3 new families in the D29/D30 layouts (line-1 `<comment> HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, a header block, a named descriptor literal -- quoted AND unquoted like D29 Makefile `X := <data>` --, an indirect use), rendered as (a) a semantic contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<role>-<field>`, 11 fields) and (b) a per-file contract (`polyglot-<lang>-<6hex>-<field>`, 13 fields incl. url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token, LYR-tagged markers). Assert 100% answered by lib.codec.v3_plan + plan_answer for underscore-free and underscore families. Stdlib only; tiny fixtures.\"\nnotes=[g for g in gaps if g['action']!='prebuild']\nfor g in notes:\n    if g['id']=='mastery-set-scope':\n        g['detail']+=\" D29 13 sets, D30 14 sets (per-file ids), first try both.\"\n    if g['id']=='timed-contract-shape-diff':\n        g['detail']+=\" D29 + D30: per-file again (TT 1833 = 1781 + 52 makefile; TT 1898 = 1833 + 65 beanshell incl. the folded JSP host), carried solver unpatched; still keep both paths for the finale.\"\n    if g['id']=='next-language-pool-roadmap':\n        g['concept']=\"forecast the next language from the timed next_language pool (7/7 D24-D30)\"\n        g['detail']=\"Hits: jsp D24, elixir D25, erlang D26, dockerfile D27, terraform_hcl D28, makefile D29, beanshell D30 (each left the pool the day it shipped; D27 semantic timed hid the pool). After D30 10 left: awk, fish, kotlin, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, xslt, zsh -- with one day left most are decoy vocabulary. Read only TODAY's auto-* expected.json `-next-language` values (older cases carry stale pools). On D31 first check whether the single grew at all (1802 + 44/55 = a language; +0 = capstone) before spending time on language forms.\"\n    if g['id']=='mastery-scale-final-days':\n        g['detail']=\"D28 12 x 1781 solve 3.5 s / submit 6.2 s; D29 13 x 1833 solve 5.7 s / submit 4.6 s (11.0 s); D30 14 x 1898 = 26572 solve 7.25 s / submit 5.9 s (14.0 s). Solve time is now growing faster than the set count -- see prebuild gap mastery-scale-bench-30k. Keep one submit (GM: up to 4 MiB of JSON per request; split only above), fork per set, never re-index nested AES zips per set.\"\n    if g['id']=='solver-lib-v3-fallback':\n        g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\"STILL OPEN after D28: the D28 solve.py\",\"STILL OPEN after D30 (not needed D29/D30 -- the carried D19 unescape read the D30 JSP host): the solve.py\")\norder=[g for g in new if g['priority']==1]+[g for g in new if g['priority']==2]\npre1=[g for g in order if g['priority']==1]; pre2=[g for g in order if g['priority']==2]\nfinal=pre1+[mlb]+pre2+notes\nout=json.dumps(final,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False)\ntxt=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in final)+\"\\n]\\n\"\nprose_end=j0\nprose=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D27 nights (see git history) and D28 night\nembedded-prior-script-dual-plan (`lib.codec.embedded_scripts`), lyr-layer-vocab-extend, pool-language-host-wrappers,\ndescriptor-decode-call-wrapper, make-recipe-inner-scripts (2nd try), change-order-anomaly (`order_anomalies`),\nhcl-resource-dependency-timeline. Corpus readers already in lib: handoff_graph/handoff_answer, corpus_links, lineage,\ncorpus_summary/corpus_answer. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\nfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\ncomposite-label-field-regime. Prebuild rules learned: only hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no `__import__`, no `tomllib`);\nkeep fixtures tiny (other lanes' slow fixtures under load have sunk script-lane attempts).\nPriority-1 order for D31 (finale; 30 languages declared complete on D30): the corpus GRAPH question the D30 prompt promised\n(bridge edge, host/execution/evidence edges, handoff target member), a capstone contract that adds only new suffixes on old\nfamilies, a 2-deep nested host, and the 15-set Mastery speed budget; then a last pool-language multi-drop, the D29\ncross-variant consensus, a marker/plan schema bump, a shipped graph evidence file, and a mixed-grammar contract.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:g0]+prose+\"```json\\n\"+txt+\"```\"+s[j1+3:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n# validate\ns2=open(p).read(); a=s2.index('```json',s2.index('## Readiness gaps')); b=s2.index('```',a+7)\nG=json.loads(s2[a+7:b]); print(len(G), all(set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for g in G))\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in G if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint('pending prebuild',len(pend),pend)\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2914,"cache_read_input_tokens":126354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2914},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804d4269-9c1b-478e-a2b8-4da32f300eac","uuid":"289a8ed7-c36c-4195-b9cb-e63dc9fe589e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:44:49.533Z","request_id":"req_011CgZdD77MApN9yZMPVQFKa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LwbTU4VTMKP1TCTkx691ni":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ng0=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nj0=s.index('```json',g0); j1=s.index('```',j0+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j0+7:j1])\nby={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nbuilt={'embedded-prior-script-dual-plan','lyr-layer-vocab-extend','pool-language-host-wr